 "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Syntax in Javascript", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about JavaScript syntax.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences With If Clauses- Affirmative Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <b>conditional sentence</b> states something that happens, will happen, could have happened or could happen depending on a condition.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Conditional clauses</b> are called like this because they talk about situations that need a condition to be true or not. There are different types of <b>conditional sentences</b> and each of them expresses in different degrees how likely it is for something to take place or how probable was it for something to occur in the past or in an unreal situation.<br/><br/>  <b>Conditional sentences</b> are composed of two clauses: the \u2018<strong>if clause</strong>' that explains the condition, and the \u2018<strong>main clause</strong>' which presents the result or consequence.<br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><b>If I had used</b> Javascript for the project, I <b>would have gotten</b> a better grade.<br/> <b>Your code will show </b>an error <b>if you forget</b> to write some symbols.</span> </br></br> Note that when the \u2018<strong>if clause</strong>' is placed after the \u2018<strong>main clause</strong>' we don't write a coma between both clauses as shown in the last example.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If I follow the syntax rules, working will be easier for me. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If the programming language is case-sensitive, you need to be aware of capital letters. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I need your help with JavaScript , I'll ask you again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had paid more attention in class, I would have understood Javascript syntax.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Breaking Down Comments in JavaScript", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "It is possible to embed comments in JavaScript without affecting the regular operations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When inputting text in JavaScript, we need to be careful with the syntax so the text and comments don't mix. This is basically done by using certain symbols to embed single or multiple line comments.<br/><br/>   JavaScript supports C- and C++- styles. If you want to insert comments in JavaScript, you can use  \u2018//' or embed the comments in between \u2018/* text */'. It is also possible to open with \u2018<!\u2014\u2018 and close it with \u2018//-->'. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "painstakingly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to do something taking great care of details  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the case of programming languages, syntax isn't very flexible and demands statements to be written painstakingly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jot something down ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take note of something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Ok, I think I'd better jot it down.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "uppercase ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the larger size of a letter usually used at the beginning of sentences or proper nouns, a synonym of \u201ccapital letter\u201d  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So I need to be careful with lower and upper case.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "semicolon ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the punctuation mark used to separate different ideas that are linked to each other, also known as this symbol \u201c;\u201d ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Statements are separated by semicolons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "be mindful of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep something in mind, to consider something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Statements are separated by semicolons. If they are in different lines, a semicolon is not needed. That's something you really need to be mindful of.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for information about tags in Javascript.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a brochure where you include 5 different tags and their functionality.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation with the tags you chose.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your presentation with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand tags in Javascript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I recognize the attributes of scripts in Javascripts. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I know what case-sensitive in javascript is.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class.", "type": "text"}]}]}